 { Again, the kings are opposing each other, albeit horizontally. The same kind of intermediate check helps White to win. } 1. { -KEY- } Rb7+ $1 ( { The indifferent } 1. Rxf7 $4 { would let the opponent prevail by the same method: } Rd1 $1 2. Ke5 c2 3. Rb7 Ka4 4. Rc7 c1=Q $11 5. Rxc1 Rxc1 6. f6 gxf6 7. gxf6 Rf1 { , and Black wins by one tempo after } 8. Ke6 Kb5 9. f7 Kc5 10. Ke7 Kd5 11. f8=Q $11 Rxf8 12. Kxf8 Ke6 $1 ) 
Ka3 2. Rxf7 Kb2 ( { Or } 2... c2 $2 3. Kc3 $1 ) 
3. Rb7+ $1 { Once more the same trick, forcing the enemy king to a worse square before taking the pawn. } Kc2 4. Rxg7 ( { White soon wins; e.g. } 4. Rxg7 Rd1 5. Ke5 Kd2 6. Rd7 Kc1 7. Rc7 c2 8. g6 Kd2 9. g7 Rg1 10. f6 ) 

