 { White appears to be in trouble, but an intermediate check helped to save the game. } 1. { -KEY- } Rd6+ $1 { Before attacking the b7-pawn, White wants to see where the black king goes. } ( { a) Both } 1. Rf7 $2 ) 
 ( { b) And } 1. Ke2 $2 { obviously failed to } Rxb4 ) 
 ( { c) While } 1. b5 $2 cxb5 2. Ke2 Kxc5 3. Kd3 Rc4 $1 { cutting off the enemy king, also wins for Black. } ) 
Kc4 ( { After } 1... Ke5 2. b5 $1 { White manages an improved version of 1 b5 above, since the black king has moved one file away from the queenside; i.e. } cxb5 3. Rb6 b4 4. Ke2 Kd5 5. Kd3 Rc4 6. Rxb7 Rc3 7. Kd2 Kxc5 8. Rc7 $1 { transposing to a drawn pawn ending. } ) 
2. Rd7 Kxb4 3. Rxb7+ Kxc5 4. Ke2 Kc4 ( { Or } 4... Rd4 5. Rb1 $1 { and the frontal attack saves a draw; e.g. } Kc4 6. Rc1 Kd5 7. Rb1 c5 8. Rd1 $1 ) 
5. Kd2 Rh2+ 6. Kc1 Kc3 7. Kb1 $1 { To the short side. } c5 8. Rg7 { White soon drew, applying the defence of the long side. } 
