 { White plans Rg7-g8, but first it makes sense to displace the enemy king. } 1. { -KEY- } Rb7+ $1 ( { Less clear is } 1. Rg7 Rh8 2. Ke4 Kc4 { when Black has an extra tempo on the game. } ) 
Ka6 2. Rg7 Rh8 { The only defence against 3.Rg8. Now the white king is ready to invade. } 3. Ke4 Kb5 4. Kf3 $1 ( { Simpler than } 4. Ke5 Kc4 5. Rd7 Rf8 $1 { cutting off the enemy king, at least for the moment. } ) 
Kc4 5. Rd7 Kd3 6. Kg4 Rxh7 { There is nothing better. } 7. Rxh7 Kxd4 8. Rd7+ $1 { One more intermediate check to force the enemy king to an inferior square. } ( { a) } 8. Kxg5 c5 9. Kf4 $1 { was also possible; } ( { but not } 9. Kxg6 $2 c4 10. Rd7 Ke3 { and Black escapes. } ) 
 ) 
 ( { b) After } 8. Rd7 { Black resigned, in view of } Kc4 9. Kf3 { bringing the king towards the most dangerous of the pawns. } ) 

 1-0

